
# ── WARN-BATCH FLUSH (2026-09-24) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Every 30 min, on EVERY box: drain this box's own warn spool
# (state/alert-warn-batch.jsonl) into ONE Telegram message. A warn spools on
# the box that raised it, so a hub-only flush would leave every project box
# (review-prs, triage, call-guard) on the inline dead-man alone. Not behind the
# hub lease: each box drains only its own spool. Deterministic jq/awk, no LLM;
# an empty spool sends nothing. Same flock as the inline dead-man in
# bin/lib/alert-state.sh, so the two never double-send.
# OFF-SWITCH CAVEAT: flags/lane-off-alert-warn-flush (or flags/all-off) also
# stops that inline dead-man, which runs the same --warn-batch. While it is set
# this box delivers NO warn; the spool silently trims oldest-first at
# ALERT_WARN_BATCH_MAX (60). Clearing it delivers what is left next tick.
# tests/alert-warn-batch-cron-test.sh.
*/30 * * * * /root/harness/bin/alert-warn-flush.sh >> /root/harness/logs/alert-digest.log 2>&1
